WEBVTT

00:01.750 --> 00:03.060
What's in it?

00:03.500 --> 00:06.560
Things that are important to Master?

00:06.560 --> 00:08.700
Is this a love letter?!

00:09.440 --> 00:11.290
Where are you three from?

00:11.290 --> 00:15.070
Um, we apologize, but we're in a hurry...

00:15.450 --> 00:16.650
You've got some nerve!

00:17.830 --> 00:21.450
Hm? I don't remember packing a box like this.

00:22.080 --> 00:24.760
Did someone give you that as a moving gift?

00:30.090 --> 00:32.760
A Strarf-model Shinki?

00:32.760 --> 00:37.120
Didn't a Strarf model win last year's tournament?

00:51.280 --> 00:52.240
What?

00:52.240 --> 00:54.590
Dad, you signed me up for a consumer review Shinki?

00:55.120 --> 00:56.290
Why?

00:57.160 --> 00:58.870
A surprise?

01:01.000 --> 01:05.080
No, I'm not saying you jumped the gun...

01:05.080 --> 01:08.520
Geez, what's our Master's dad thinking?

01:08.520 --> 01:10.750
He's already got us three here.

01:10.750 --> 01:14.720
And he gets another brand new Shinki?

01:16.480 --> 01:19.150
I wouldn't mind if things were a bit livelier around here.

01:26.980 --> 01:26.980
{OP}

01:27.440 --> 01:29.870
It shines

01:29.870 --> 01:33.930
My singing voice is endless

01:33.930 --> 01:40.510
My eternal pledge is only for you

01:40.510 --> 01:47.250
I wonder if you're your usual self

01:47.250 --> 01:52.730
I'll sparkle with you

01:52.730 --> 01:55.740
Install dream

02:00.630 --> 02:05.620
The arms of the clock advance

02:06.850 --> 02:12.040
and with them so does time

02:12.040 --> 02:19.200
When you are sad, I open my tiny arms

02:19.200 --> 02:25.550
and embrace you

02:27.540 --> 02:29.870
Fly

02:29.870 --> 02:34.150
My singing voice is tender

02:34.150 --> 02:40.530
I can remember your shape

02:40.530 --> 02:43.530
and that wasn't brought about by a program

02:43.530 --> 02:47.140
Let us experience

02:47.140 --> 02:52.830
the turmoil in my heart together

02:52.830 --> 02:55.900
Install dream

02:56.900 --> 03:01.780
The Secret Ingredient Smells Like Gunpowder!

02:56.900 --> 03:01.780
The Secret Ingredient Smells Like Gunpowder!

02:56.900 --> 03:01.780
The Secret Ingredient Smells Like Gunpowder!

03:03.520 --> 03:06.150
Now, about your name...

03:07.600 --> 03:10.070
Hi... na.

03:12.630 --> 03:13.980
Registration complete.

03:15.830 --> 03:17.720
My name is Hina.

03:17.720 --> 03:20.340
It is a pleasure to meet you, Master.

03:21.100 --> 03:23.680
Welcome, Hina.

03:23.680 --> 03:24.800
Hina?

03:25.430 --> 03:26.310
Yeah.

03:26.870 --> 03:30.490
She just activated, so she's still like a baby.

03:30.960 --> 03:34.440
You three should introduce her to the place.

03:40.470 --> 03:41.490
Here you go.

03:49.370 --> 03:52.500
My name is Ann. Let's be friends!

03:52.500 --> 03:54.100
My name is Lene.

03:54.560 --> 03:57.080
And this is Ines.

03:57.080 --> 03:59.530
She's configured to be my little sister!

03:59.530 --> 04:01.220
Don't call me configured!

04:13.350 --> 04:14.490
Nice to meet you.

04:16.530 --> 04:18.610
What kinda greeting is <i>that</i>?

04:21.120 --> 04:23.610
I wish to see your strength.

04:24.570 --> 04:27.460
We don't do that around here.

04:28.650 --> 04:32.100
Looks like I'm gonna have to lay down some ground rules.

04:32.100 --> 04:33.000
Got it?

04:33.000 --> 04:35.620
First, Rule #1!

04:36.230 --> 04:38.640
You may not go to sleep before Master does!

04:38.640 --> 04:40.010
What did you change it to?

04:40.010 --> 04:42.470
An old Japanese-style room!

04:40.140 --> 04:41.560
Rule #2!

04:41.560 --> 04:43.880
You may not wake up after Master does!

04:42.470 --> 04:43.880
It feels warm, doesn't it?

04:44.420 --> 04:45.910
Rule #3!

04:45.230 --> 04:47.640
I think I have a better idea.

04:45.910 --> 04:47.640
Be clean at all times!

04:48.960 --> 04:50.520
It doesn't matter if you're not made for cleaning.

04:51.200 --> 04:52.480
 And Rule #4!

04:52.480 --> 04:53.020
Fine, then.

04:54.580 --> 04:56.270
This may calm you down.

04:56.910 --> 04:58.270
Wait, why are we underground?

04:58.570 --> 05:02.200
I mean, are you even listening?

05:02.960 --> 05:05.400
How about we try the middle button?

05:09.980 --> 05:12.170
What kinda middle is <i>this</i>?

05:13.860 --> 05:16.370
So uh, yeah.

05:16.790 --> 05:19.530
I'll tell you all about Master.

05:20.670 --> 05:24.520
When he was younger, he lived in this very house,

05:24.520 --> 05:27.470
and I was right there with him!

05:26.690 --> 05:29.510
That's enough, Miss Childhood Friend.

05:29.810 --> 05:34.900
He used to live overseas due to his father's occupation,

05:34.900 --> 05:38.770
but he moved back to Japan to enter high school.

05:38.770 --> 05:43.200
And since we just finished unpacking his luggage today,

05:43.200 --> 05:45.940
our wonderful life with Master can...

05:47.310 --> 05:50.230
Hm? Um, are you listening?

05:50.230 --> 05:51.290
Hello!

05:53.910 --> 05:59.840
I'd heard that the Eukrante that's always by the school got her butt kicked recently,

05:59.840 --> 06:02.730
but I never thought the paw-petrators would be right next door! {She's a cat, so she uses cat jokes.}

06:05.180 --> 06:06.050
I know!

06:06.050 --> 06:10.430
We should give Master a gift to congratulate him entering high school!

06:10.430 --> 06:13.160
Ooh, good idea.

06:14.450 --> 06:17.980
But what should we give him?

06:18.810 --> 06:20.480
Hina, what do you think?

06:22.690 --> 06:24.480
Do not call me by that name.

06:24.870 --> 06:29.740
Why? Master went through all the trouble of making it for you.

06:31.010 --> 06:33.240
The only one allowed to use it is Master!

06:33.770 --> 06:36.680
I-In that case, what should we call you?

06:36.680 --> 06:37.960
Strarf will do.

06:37.960 --> 06:39.870
Well then, Strarf,

06:39.870 --> 06:43.250
what do you think Master would like?

06:43.970 --> 06:45.960
A tournament championship.

06:47.300 --> 06:50.010
Or perhaps the strongest weaponry available.

06:50.800 --> 06:53.650
I don't think he'd like those too much.

06:54.320 --> 06:55.260
Why?

06:56.350 --> 06:59.140
Our Master's not into battling.

07:05.230 --> 07:08.690
Wh-What was that for?

07:10.150 --> 07:11.370
Something is here.

07:15.380 --> 07:17.200
Is there a mouse?

07:24.470 --> 07:27.490
Do I look like a mouse to you?

07:27.490 --> 07:29.870
She's pretty brash for a newcomer.

07:29.870 --> 07:34.350
You're supposed to give your new neighbors soba when you move, not rain death upon them!

07:39.640 --> 07:41.810
What's all the noise for?

07:44.560 --> 07:47.850
Nothing at all! It was probably just a mouse.

07:47.850 --> 07:48.820
Hehe, yeah!

07:49.330 --> 07:50.540
And Hina—

07:50.540 --> 07:53.740
I mean, Strarf here got a little trigger happy.

07:56.920 --> 07:57.790
Master.

08:01.080 --> 08:04.880
Master, do you truly have no interest in Shinki Battling?

08:04.880 --> 08:05.900
Ah...

08:06.640 --> 08:08.380
well, battles are dangerous.

08:15.140 --> 08:18.090
Ah, that means supper's ready!

08:19.790 --> 08:21.470
I'll help you!

08:21.470 --> 08:24.920
Geez Master, didn't you have frozen pizza last night?

08:53.380 --> 08:55.260
Is this everyone?

08:55.260 --> 08:59.140
Strarf said she would be going to sleep early.

09:01.640 --> 09:03.970
I'm pretty sleepy too...

09:03.970 --> 09:07.370
What're we gonna talk about this late at night?

09:08.820 --> 09:10.400
The high school entrance gift!

09:10.400 --> 09:13.560
I thought of a good surprise for Master!

09:14.020 --> 09:16.160
We'll all make him a feast!

09:17.230 --> 09:18.350
A feast?

09:19.030 --> 09:20.800
Y-You can't mean...

09:20.800 --> 09:23.080
we'll be <i>cooking</i>?!

09:23.080 --> 09:25.270
Cooking?! But that's...

09:29.310 --> 09:32.320
"Another Shinki Cooking Accident!"

09:32.320 --> 09:34.840
"This one slipped on oil and fell into the pot!"

09:34.840 --> 09:36.800
"She was deep-fried!"

09:42.600 --> 09:44.990
"Following the incident..."

09:44.990 --> 09:49.350
"Ms. S, who once took a bad trip through a blender, said..."

09:49.350 --> 09:54.030
"'Having Shinkis cook food... is a recipe for disaster!'"

10:02.640 --> 10:05.440
M-Maybe this isn't such a good idea...

10:06.120 --> 10:07.200
But think!

10:07.200 --> 10:10.230
If Master comes home to a splendid home-cooked meal instead of a TV dinner,

10:10.230 --> 10:12.880
just imagine how happy he'd be!

10:12.880 --> 10:14.050
Master would be...

10:14.050 --> 10:15.630
happy?!

10:20.640 --> 10:21.980
All right!

10:21.980 --> 10:23.270
We're doin' this thing!

10:23.270 --> 10:26.770
If we all work together, neither the devil nor food preparation can stand in our way!

10:26.770 --> 10:29.380
With that done, let's pick out our menu!

10:29.380 --> 10:30.680
We're totally doing Japanese cuisine!

10:30.680 --> 10:34.090
Sashimi, tempura, sukiyaki, geisha...

10:33.480 --> 10:34.530
Exactly!

10:34.530 --> 10:37.910
Well then, let's order our ingredients!

10:37.910 --> 10:40.410
Keep it within next week's food budget!

10:40.410 --> 10:45.580
Yeah, yeah. Okay, we need some shrimp, octopus, tuna...

10:45.580 --> 10:47.240
Added to the cart!

10:47.240 --> 10:49.160
I want to make a cake, too!

10:49.160 --> 10:50.920
How about omelette rice?

11:04.930 --> 11:09.220
<i>Were we not created to fight?</i>

11:25.120 --> 11:26.700
The time is ripe!

11:26.700 --> 11:28.870
Now, our battle begins!

11:29.490 --> 11:30.470
Hm?

11:30.470 --> 11:31.750
Where's Strarf?

11:32.170 --> 11:36.050
She said she couldn't help with anything but battling, so she passed.

11:37.320 --> 11:40.050
Time's short, so let's get started!

11:42.910 --> 11:45.510
So, we'll start with...

11:45.510 --> 11:47.850
Oh, wait just a moment!

11:47.850 --> 11:49.520
We'll start with <i>this</i>!

11:50.210 --> 11:52.740
Huh? Apron Armor?

11:53.520 --> 11:56.770
If you wear this over your figure,

11:56.770 --> 11:58.940
young boys will be overjoyed!

12:00.600 --> 12:02.440
So, a PVC apron?

12:02.440 --> 12:04.410
Well then... {oh god my dick}

12:05.690 --> 12:06.950
Wait, wait!

12:07.200 --> 12:10.080
There's still one more thing to do!

12:10.080 --> 12:12.030
What else is there?

12:12.030 --> 12:15.580
Master's gonna get home before we even get started!

12:16.050 --> 12:17.830
This is the one thing we can't skip!

12:17.830 --> 12:22.840
Antibacterial spray is an essential part of preparation!

12:35.480 --> 12:37.810
Onward! To cooking!

12:39.730 --> 12:41.860
I'll wash the rice!

12:48.270 --> 12:51.330
That'll take days!

12:55.480 --> 12:56.230
Shrimp beard!

12:56.230 --> 12:57.560
Don't play with your food!

13:02.420 --> 13:03.510
Got it!

13:06.080 --> 13:09.010
Ah! That's my armor!

13:10.490 --> 13:12.630
We're making great time!

13:12.630 --> 13:15.380
This isn't so dangerous after all.

13:30.260 --> 13:32.700
It's a bit too salty. {Like me after playing 3s ;_;}

13:32.700 --> 13:34.560
Here I go! {Shinki asses are one of the strongest weapons known to man}

13:59.730 --> 14:02.480
What are those three doing?

14:04.950 --> 14:07.680
I dunno, but we should get in their way!

14:07.680 --> 14:09.460
As revenge for yesterday's cat-tack.

14:10.610 --> 14:13.120
Time to pounce, Mini Meowchines!

14:16.540 --> 14:18.500
Shoot, it's getting dark.

14:18.500 --> 14:19.620
Pick it up, guys!

14:20.100 --> 14:22.880
Once we're done... with this...

14:22.880 --> 14:26.420
We'll heat the pumpkin in the microwave...

14:26.420 --> 14:29.880
so we can get a knife in... and cut it more easily...

14:50.580 --> 14:52.080
Victory is sweet!

14:52.080 --> 14:53.200
Yay!

14:53.670 --> 14:55.750
All right, on with the plan!

14:57.550 --> 14:59.540
Oh boy...

15:03.120 --> 15:04.820
We have to clean this up, quick!

15:04.820 --> 15:06.210
Y-Yeah.

15:06.210 --> 15:08.710
I brought a vacuum cleaner! {The vacuum cleaner is lighter than the pumpkin?}

15:11.570 --> 15:13.090
{よいしょ}

15:34.030 --> 15:35.660
Get to the breaker!

15:36.470 --> 15:37.410
Where is it?

15:38.010 --> 15:40.000
I'll take care of it!

16:38.330 --> 16:39.830
Lene!

16:43.460 --> 16:46.100
What... <i>is</i> this?

16:50.780 --> 16:52.110
What?

16:56.450 --> 16:57.580
Ines!

17:33.270 --> 17:34.630
What the...

17:46.610 --> 17:48.080
Mission complete!

17:49.210 --> 17:52.120
Consider it your punishment for not bringing soba!

18:10.980 --> 18:12.570
Strarf?

18:13.850 --> 18:15.080
Stand down.

18:49.560 --> 18:51.430
You saved us...

18:53.570 --> 18:55.940
Come back, Mini Meowchines!

18:57.140 --> 19:00.450
I'll test my strength on you. Come!

19:00.450 --> 19:01.950
Shut up!

19:01.950 --> 19:03.950
Shutupshutupshutupshutupshutup!

19:03.950 --> 19:06.830
And eat... your veggies!

19:15.560 --> 19:16.250
Got it!

19:22.060 --> 19:24.350
Such obstacles are hardly worth my time.

19:25.280 --> 19:27.100
Here comes the main course!

19:27.100 --> 19:29.520
Would you like a side with that?

19:30.850 --> 19:32.180
Slice it here!

19:37.220 --> 19:39.090
Wow, it's still mov— {This doesn't kill the fish}

19:42.570 --> 19:44.320
Now I'm <i>berry</i> mad!

19:56.320 --> 19:57.670
Wow.

19:58.410 --> 20:00.570
We're out of ammo!

20:01.300 --> 20:03.500
So it's come down to this...

20:04.880 --> 20:06.750
Catreat!

20:06.750 --> 20:08.560
I'll remeowmber this!

20:11.300 --> 20:13.570
Thank you, Strarf!

20:15.810 --> 20:17.370
Think nothing of it.

20:17.370 --> 20:20.450
We were all built for combat, after all.

20:24.460 --> 20:27.200
Hey! Get moving, Master'll be here any minute!

20:27.200 --> 20:28.740
Oh no!

20:28.740 --> 20:30.200
Strarf, help us!

20:30.700 --> 20:32.550
W-Wait...

20:37.580 --> 20:39.590
Hurry, hurry!

20:39.590 --> 20:41.090
What time is it?

20:41.650 --> 20:43.180
Why must I be forced to...

20:43.840 --> 20:46.220
This'll finish the omelette rice!

20:47.500 --> 20:48.970
For what reason?

20:49.250 --> 20:51.480
And the finishing touches...

20:52.540 --> 20:53.730
I'm home!

21:01.450 --> 21:03.220
And we're... done!

